reviews.review:
EDIT: Whoa, what a polising. I tried the game today, after more than a month, it's super smooth now, levels are destructible, everything is even better and difficulty is also tuned. A very good game, I can easily see this one in a VR arcade.

VR Invaders is different, and in my opinion better, than the vast majority of wave shooters for many reasons:

1) it has a progression, eight stages with different locations, bosses and powerups: you can continue, but if you stop the next time you will restart (just like a coinop);
2) the graphics is real good;
3) formations reminds me a lot Galaga, similiar paths and better score if you hit all of them in a combo;
4) it includes a bullet time mode, extremely useful and quite spectacular if well used.

The game has a few bugs at the moment, but it's yet well playable. To be able to progress into new stages, aiming to finish the game, makes an huge difference for me.
